---@field deploymentArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the initial daemon deployment. This deployment places daemon tasks on each container instance of the specified capacity providers.

---@class aws.ecs.CreateExpressGatewayServiceRequest
---@field executionRoleArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the task execution role that grants the Amazon ECS container agent permission to make Amazon Web Services API calls on your behalf. This role is required for Amazon ECS to pull container images from Amazon ECR, send container logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs, and retrieve sensitive data from Amazon Web Services Systems Manager Parameter Store or Amazon Web Services ...
---@field infrastructureRoleArn aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the infrastructure role that grants Amazon ECS permission to create and manage Amazon Web Services resources on your behalf for the Express service. This role is used to provision and manage Application Load Balancers, target groups, security groups, auto-scaling policies, and other Amazon Web Services infrastructure components.
---@field serviceName? aws.ecs.String The name of the Express service. This name must be unique within the specified cluster and can contain up to 255 letters (uppercase and lowercase), numbers, underscores, and hyphens. The name is used to identify the service in the Amazon ECS console and API operations.
---@field cluster? aws.ecs.String The short name or full Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the cluster on which to create the Express service. If you do not specify a cluster, the default cluster is assumed.
---@field healthCheckPath? aws.ecs.String The path on the container that the Application Load Balancer uses for health checks. This should be a valid HTTP endpoint that returns a successful response (HTTP 200) when the application is healthy.
---@field primaryContainer? aws.ecs.ExpressGatewayContainer The primary container configuration for the Express service. This defines the main application container that will receive traffic from the Application Load Balancer.
---@field taskRoleArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IAM role that containers in this task can assume. This role allows your application code to access other Amazon Web Services services securely.
---@field networkConfiguration? aws.ecs.ExpressGatewayServiceNetworkConfiguration The network configuration for the Express service tasks. This specifies the VPC subnets and security groups for the tasks.
---@field cpu? aws.ecs.String The number of CPU units used by the task. This parameter determines the CPU allocation for each task in the Express service. The default value for an Express service is 256 (.25 vCPU).
---@field memory? aws.ecs.String The amount of memory (in MiB) used by the task. This parameter determines the memory allocation for each task in the Express service. The default value for an express service is 512 MiB.
---@field cpuArchitecture? aws.ecs.ExpressCpuArchitecture|string The CPU architecture that the task runs on. If you don't specify a value, the default is X86_64.
---@field scalingTarget? aws.ecs.ExpressGatewayScalingTarget The auto-scaling configuration for the Express service. This defines how the service automatically adjusts the number of running tasks based on demand.
---@field tags? aws.ecs.Tags The metadata that you apply to the Express service to help categorize and organize it. Each tag consists of a key and an optional value. You can apply up to 50 tags to a service.
---@field taskDefinitionArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of a task definition to use to create the Express Gateway service. This allows you to manage your own task definition, giving you more control over the service configuration such as adding sidecar containers.

---@class aws.ecs.CreateExpressGatewayServiceResponse
---@field service? aws.ecs.ECSExpressGatewayService The full description of your Express service following the create operation.

---@class aws.ecs.CreateGatewayRequest
---@field name aws.ecs.String The name for the gateway. The name must be unique within your account and can be up to 255 characters.
---@field infrastructureRoleArn aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IAM role that the gateway assumes to create and manage infrastructure on your behalf.
---@field clientToken? aws.ecs.String A unique, case-sensitive identifier that you provide to ensure that the operation completes no more than one time. If this token matches a previous request, the service ignores the request, but does not return an error.
---@field deletionProtection? aws.ecs.BoxedBoolean Specifies whether to enable deletion protection for the gateway. When enabled, the gateway can't be deleted, and the gateway propagates this setting to the load balancers it manages. The default is true.
---@field configuration aws.ecs.GatewayConfiguration The type-specific configuration for the gateway. Exactly one configuration variant must be set, and it determines the gateway type. For example, hostSharedAlb configures a gateway that uses Application Load Balancers with host-based routing.
---@field tags? aws.ecs.Tags The metadata that you apply to the gateway to help you categorize and organize it. Each tag consists of a key and an optional value. Depending on propagateTags, these tags can be applied to the infrastructure the gateway manages.
---@field propagateTags? aws.ecs.PropagateGatewayTags|string Specifies whether to propagate the tags from the gateway to the infrastructure that the gateway manages. The default is GATEWAY.

---@class aws.ecs.CreateGatewayResponse
