---Information about a daemon revision. A daemon revision is a snapshot of the daemon's configuration at the time a deployment was initiated.
---@class aws.ecs.DaemonRevision
---@field daemonRevisionArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the daemon revision.
---@field clusterArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the cluster that hosts the daemon.
---@field daemonArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the daemon for this revision.
---@field daemonTaskDefinitionArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the daemon task definition used by this revision.
---@field createdAt? aws.ecs.Timestamp The Unix timestamp for the time when the daemon revision was created.
---@field containerImages? aws.ecs.DaemonContainerImages The container images used by the daemon revision.
---@field propagateTags? aws.ecs.DaemonPropagateTags Specifies whether tags are propagated from the daemon to the daemon tasks.
---@field enableECSManagedTags? aws.ecs.BoxedBoolean Specifies whether Amazon ECS managed tags are turned on for the daemon tasks.
---@field enableExecuteCommand? aws.ecs.BoxedBoolean Specifies whether the execute command functionality is turned on for the daemon tasks.
---@field critical? aws.ecs.BoxedBoolean If the critical parameter of this daemon revision is true, and the daemon task fails, stops, or becomes unhealthy, Amazon ECS drains the container instance and stops the other tasks running on it. If the parameter is false, the daemon task failure doesn't affect the other tasks on the instance, and doesn't block instance registration. The default value is true.

