---@field updatedAt? aws.ecs.Timestamp The Unix timestamp for the time when the daemon was last updated.

---The details of a daemon task definition. A daemon task definition is a template that describes the containers that form a daemon. Daemons deploy cross-cutting software agents independently across your Amazon ECS infrastructure.
---@class aws.ecs.DaemonTaskDefinition
---@field daemonTaskDefinitionArn? aws.ecs.String The full Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the daemon task definition.
---@field family? aws.ecs.String The name of a family that this daemon task definition is registered to.
---@field revision aws.ecs.Integer The revision of the daemon task in a particular family. The revision is a version number of a daemon task definition in a family. When you register a daemon task definition for the first time, the revision is 1. Each time that you register a new revision of a daemon task definition in the same family, the revision value always increases by one.
---@field taskRoleArn? aws.ecs.String The short name or full Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IAM role that grants containers in the daemon task permission to call Amazon Web Services APIs on your behalf.
---@field executionRoleArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the task execution role that grants the Amazon ECS container agent permission to make Amazon Web Services API calls on your behalf.
---@field containerDefinitions? aws.ecs.DaemonContainerDefinitionList A list of container definitions in JSON format that describe the containers that make up the daemon task.
---@field volumes? aws.ecs.DaemonVolumeList The list of data volume definitions for the daemon task.
---@field cpu? aws.ecs.String The number of CPU units used by the daemon task.
---@field memory? aws.ecs.String The amount of memory (in MiB) used by the daemon task.
---@field status? aws.ecs.DaemonTaskDefinitionStatus The status of the daemon task definition. The valid values are ACTIVE, DELETE_IN_PROGRESS, and DELETED.
---@field registeredAt? aws.ecs.Timestamp The Unix timestamp for the time when the daemon task definition was registered.
---@field deleteRequestedAt? aws.ecs.Timestamp The Unix timestamp for the time when the daemon task definition delete was requested.
---@field registeredBy? aws.ecs.String The principal that registered the daemon task definition.
---@field pidMode? aws.ecs.DaemonPidMode The PID namespace mode for the daemon. The valid values are none and shared. The default is none.
---@field ipcMode? aws.ecs.DaemonIpcMode The IPC namespace mode for the daemon. The valid values are none and shared. The default is none.

---@alias aws.ecs.DaemonTaskDefinitionRevisionFilter "LAST_REGISTERED"

---@alias aws.ecs.DaemonTaskDefinitionStatus "ACTIVE"|"DELETE_IN_PROGRESS"|"DELETED"

---@alias aws.ecs.DaemonTaskDefinitionStatusFilter "ACTIVE"|"DELETE_IN_PROGRESS"|"ALL"

---@alias aws.ecs.DaemonTaskDefinitionSummaries aws.ecs.DaemonTaskDefinitionSummary[]

