---The launch template configuration for Amazon ECS Managed Instances. This defines how Amazon ECS launches Amazon EC2 instances, including the instance profile for your tasks, network and storage configuration, capacity options, and instance requirements for flexible instance type selection.
---@class aws.ecs.InstanceLaunchTemplate
---@field ec2InstanceProfileArn aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the instance profile that Amazon ECS applies to Amazon ECS Managed Instances. This instance profile must include the necessary permissions for your tasks to access Amazon Web Services services and resources.
---@field networkConfiguration aws.ecs.ManagedInstancesNetworkConfiguration The network configuration for Amazon ECS Managed Instances. This specifies the subnets and security groups that instances use for network connectivity.
---@field storageConfiguration? aws.ecs.ManagedInstancesStorageConfiguration The storage configuration for Amazon ECS Managed Instances. This defines the data volume properties for the instances.
---@field localStorageConfiguration? aws.ecs.ManagedInstancesLocalStorageConfiguration The local storage configuration for Amazon ECS Managed Instances. This defines how ECS uses instance store volumes available on the container instance.
---@field monitoring? aws.ecs.ManagedInstancesMonitoringOptions|string CloudWatch provides two categories of monitoring: basic monitoring and detailed monitoring. By default, your managed instance is configured for basic monitoring. You can optionally enable detailed monitoring to help you more quickly identify and act on operational issues. You can enable or turn off detailed monitoring at launch or when the managed instance is running or stopped. For more informati...
---@field capacityOptionType? aws.ecs.CapacityOptionType|string The capacity option type. This determines whether Amazon ECS launches On-Demand, Spot or Capacity Reservation Instances for your managed instance capacity provider.
---@field instanceMetadataTagsPropagation? aws.ecs.BoxedBoolean Determines whether tags are propagated to the instance metadata service (IMDS) for Amazon EC2 instances launched by the Managed Instances capacity provider. When enabled, all tags associated with the instance are available through the instance metadata service. When disabled, tags are not propagated to IMDS.
---@field instanceRequirements? aws.ecs.InstanceRequirementsRequest The instance requirements. You can specify:
---@field fipsEnabled? aws.ecs.BoxedBoolean Determines whether to enable FIPS 140-2 validated cryptographic modules on EC2 instances launched by the capacity provider. If true, instances use FIPS-compliant cryptographic algorithms and modules for enhanced security compliance. If false, instances use standard cryptographic implementations.
---@field capacityReservations? aws.ecs.CapacityReservationRequest Capacity reservation specifications. You can specify:
---@field nitroEnclavesEnabled? aws.ecs.BoxedBoolean Specifies whether instances that this capacity provider launches have Nitro Sandbox enabled. Enable this setting to run tasks that use the ISOLATED_SANDBOX or CONFIDENTIAL_SANDBOX isolation mode.

