---The configuration for the Amazon EBS volume that Amazon ECS creates and manages on your behalf. These settings are used to create each Amazon EBS volume, with one volume created for each task in the service. For information about the supported launch types and operating systems, see Supported operating systems and launch types in the Amazon Elastic Container Service Developer Guide.
---@class aws.ecs.ServiceManagedEBSVolumeConfiguration
---@field encrypted? aws.ecs.BoxedBoolean Indicates whether the volume should be encrypted. If you turn on Region-level Amazon EBS encryption by default but set this value as false, the setting is overridden and the volume is encrypted with the KMS key specified for Amazon EBS encryption by default. This parameter maps 1:1 with the Encrypted parameter of the CreateVolume API in the Amazon EC2 API Reference.
---@field kmsKeyId? aws.ecs.EBSKMSKeyId The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) identifier of the Amazon Web Services Key Management Service key to use for Amazon EBS encryption. When a key is specified using this parameter, it overrides Amazon EBS default encryption or any KMS key that you specified for cluster-level managed storage encryption. This parameter maps 1:1 with the KmsKeyId parameter of the CreateVolume API in the Amazon EC2 API Ref...
---@field volumeType? aws.ecs.EBSVolumeType The volume type. This parameter maps 1:1 with the VolumeType parameter of the CreateVolume API in the Amazon EC2 API Reference. For more information, see Amazon EBS volume types in the Amazon EC2 User Guide.
---@field sizeInGiB? aws.ecs.BoxedInteger The size of the volume in GiB. You must specify either a volume size or a snapshot ID. If you specify a snapshot ID, the snapshot size is used for the volume size by default. You can optionally specify a volume size greater than or equal to the snapshot size. This parameter maps 1:1 with the Size parameter of the CreateVolume API in the Amazon EC2 API Reference.
---@field snapshotId? aws.ecs.EBSSnapshotId The snapshot that Amazon ECS uses to create volumes for attachment to tasks maintained by the service. You must specify either snapshotId or sizeInGiB in your volume configuration. This parameter maps 1:1 with the SnapshotId parameter of the CreateVolume API in the Amazon EC2 API Reference.
---@field volumeInitializationRate? aws.ecs.BoxedInteger The rate, in MiB/s, at which data is fetched from a snapshot of an existing EBS volume to create new volumes for attachment to the tasks maintained by the service. This property can be specified only if you specify a snapshotId. For more information, see Initialize Amazon EBS volumes in the Amazon EBS User Guide.
---@field iops? aws.ecs.BoxedInteger The number of I/O operations per second (IOPS). For gp3, io1, and io2 volumes, this represents the number of IOPS that are provisioned for the volume. For gp2 volumes, this represents the baseline performance of the volume and the rate at which the volume accumulates I/O credits for bursting.
---@field throughput? aws.ecs.BoxedInteger The throughput to provision for a volume, in MiB/s, with a maximum of 1,000 MiB/s. This parameter maps 1:1 with the Throughput parameter of the CreateVolume API in the Amazon EC2 API Reference.
---@field tagSpecifications? aws.ecs.EBSTagSpecifications The tags to apply to the volume. Amazon ECS applies service-managed tags by default. This parameter maps 1:1 with the TagSpecifications.N parameter of the CreateVolume API in the Amazon EC2 API Reference.
---@field roleArn aws.ecs.IAMRoleArn The ARN of the IAM role to associate with this volume. This is the Amazon ECS infrastructure IAM role that is used to manage your Amazon Web Services infrastructure. We recommend using the Amazon ECS-managed AmazonECSInfrastructureRolePolicyForVolumes IAM policy with this role. For more information, see Amazon ECS infrastructure IAM role in the Amazon ECS Developer Guide.
---@field filesystemType? aws.ecs.TaskFilesystemType|string The filesystem type for the volume. For volumes created from a snapshot, you must specify the same filesystem type that the volume was using when the snapshot was created. If there is a filesystem type mismatch, the tasks will fail to start.

---@alias aws.ecs.ServiceRegistries aws.ecs.ServiceRegistry[]

---The details for the service registry.
---@class aws.ecs.ServiceRegistry
---@field registryArn? aws.ecs.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the service registry. The currently supported service registry is Cloud Map. For more information, see CreateService.
---@field port? aws.ecs.BoxedInteger The port value used if your service discovery service specified an SRV record. This field might be used if both the awsvpc network mode and SRV records are used.
---@field containerName? aws.ecs.String The container name value to be used for your service discovery service. It's already specified in the task definition. If the task definition that your service task specifies uses the bridge or host network mode, you must specify a containerName and containerPort combination from the task definition. If the task definition that your service task specifies uses the awsvpc network mode and a type SR...
---@field containerPort? aws.ecs.BoxedInteger The port value to be used for your service discovery service. It's already specified in the task definition. If the task definition your service task specifies uses the bridge or host network mode, you must specify a containerName and containerPort combination from the task definition. If the task definition your service task specifies uses the awsvpc network mode and a type SRV DNS record is used...

---Information about the service revision.
---@class aws.ecs.ServiceRevision
---@field serviceRevisionArn? aws.ecs.String The ARN of the service revision.
---@field serviceArn? aws.ecs.String The ARN of the service for the service revision.
---@field clusterArn? aws.ecs.String The ARN of the cluster that hosts the service.
---@field taskDefinition? aws.ecs.String The task definition the service revision uses.
---@field capacityProviderStrategy? aws.ecs.CapacityProviderStrategy The capacity provider strategy the service revision uses.
---@field launchType? aws.ecs.LaunchType The launch type the service revision uses.
---@field platformVersion? aws.ecs.String For the Fargate launch type, the platform version the service revision uses.
---@field platformFamily? aws.ecs.String The platform family the service revision uses.
---@field loadBalancers? aws.ecs.LoadBalancers The load balancers the service revision uses.
---@field serviceRegistries? aws.ecs.ServiceRegistries The service registries (for Service Discovery) the service revision uses.
---@field networkConfiguration? aws.ecs.NetworkConfiguration
---@field containerImages? aws.ecs.ContainerImages The container images the service revision uses.
---@field guardDutyEnabled aws.ecs.Boolean Indicates whether Runtime Monitoring is turned on.
---@field serviceConnectConfiguration? aws.ecs.ServiceConnectConfiguration
---@field volumeConfigurations? aws.ecs.ServiceVolumeConfigurations The volumes that are configured at deployment that the service revision uses.
---@field fargateEphemeralStorage? aws.ecs.DeploymentEphemeralStorage
---@field createdAt? aws.ecs.Timestamp The time that the service revision was created. The format is yyyy-mm-dd HH:mm:ss.SSSSS.
---@field vpcLatticeConfigurations? aws.ecs.VpcLatticeConfigurations The VPC Lattice configuration for the service revision.
---@field resolvedConfiguration? aws.ecs.ResolvedConfiguration The resolved configuration for the service revision which contains the actual resources your service revision uses, such as which target groups serve traffic.
---@field ecsManagedResources? aws.ecs.ECSManagedResources The resources created and managed by Amazon ECS when you create an Express service for Amazon ECS.
---@field overrides? aws.ecs.ServiceRevisionOverrides The effective runtime overrides that Amazon ECS applies to this service revision. This value is present only when Amazon ECS detects a difference between the task definition and the actual runtime configuration.
---@field gatewayConnectors? aws.ecs.GatewayConnectorList The gateway connectors that are associated with the service revision.
---@field monitoring? aws.ecs.MonitoringConfiguration The optional monitoring configuration for the service, which defines the resolution for the service-level CPUUtilization and MemoryUtilization Amazon CloudWatch metrics. When not specified, Amazon ECS uses the default resolution of 60 seconds.

---The time when Amazon ECS removes the source revisions' tasks relative to deployment completion. When set to BLOCKING, Amazon ECS removes the previous tasks before completing the deployment. When set to DEFERRED, Amazon ECS completes the deployment first and removes the previous tasks in the background.
